    prompt: "An Eulerian path covers every **edge** exactly once. Unlike Hamiltonian paths, it has a cheap test: all edges must be in one connected piece, and the number of **odd-degree** vertices must be `0` or `2`.\n\nReturn `True` if the undirected graph has an Eulerian path. A graph with no edges counts as `True`.\n\nA path graph has two odd vertices; a triangle has none; a star with three arms has four.",
