    prompt: "KL divergence measures the extra bits you pay for encoding reality `p` using a model `q`. It is zero only when the two agree, and it is **not symmetric**.\n\nReturn `sum(p_i * log2(p_i / q_i))` in bits. Terms where `p_i` is zero contribute nothing. If any `q_i` is zero where `p_i` is positive the divergence is infinite, so return `None`.",
