    estimatedMinutes: 12,
    prompt: "Algebraically equivalent expressions behave differently in finite precision. Softmax is the classic case: `exp(1000)` overflows, but subtracting the maximum first changes nothing mathematically and everything numerically.\n\nReturn the softmax of `logits`, shifted by the maximum for stability. An empty list returns `[]`.",
    exportName: "stable_softmax",
    scaffolds: { L1: "import math\n\ndef stable_softmax(logits):\n    pass", L2: "import math\n\ndef stable_softmax(logits):\n    pass", L3: "import math\n\ndef stable_softmax(logits):\n    pass", L4: "" },
