    prompt: "k-fold cross-validation splits the data into `k` parts and uses each one as validation exactly once, so every example is scored by a model that never saw it.\n\nReturn the list of `(train_indices, validation_indices)` pairs for `n` examples split into `k` contiguous folds. Return `[]` when `k` is below 2 or above `n`.\n\nEach index must appear in validation exactly once across all folds.",
    exportName: "k_fold_indices",
    scaffolds: { L1: "def k_fold_indices(n, k):\n    pass", L2: "def k_fold_indices(n, k):\n    pass", L3: "def k_fold_indices(n, k):\n    pass", L4: "" },
