    prompt: "Softmax makes classes **compete**: raising one logit lowers everyone else's probability, because the outputs must sum to one. That is what separates multiclass from independent binary classifiers.\n\nReturn the predicted class index for `logits` — the position of the largest value. Break ties by the **smallest** index. An empty list returns `None`.\n\nSoftmax is monotone, so the largest logit is always the predicted class; you never need to exponentiate to decide.",
