    prompt: "Naive Bayes multiplies a class prior by per-feature likelihoods. A feature never seen with a class gives a likelihood of zero, which annihilates the whole product — so **Laplace smoothing** adds a pseudo-count to every option.\n\nReturn the smoothed likelihood `(count + alpha) / (total + alpha * options)`.\n\nWith `alpha = 1`, a never-observed feature still gets a small non-zero probability.",
    exportName: "smoothed_likelihood",
